  "note": "Run on the live AwwO, in the operator’s own account and workspace, on 2026-10-26, every agent on Claude Opus 5.5 working in its own sandbox computer. The film answers an Opus 5.5 video prompt by Jurly (x.com/jurlycat/status/2110426202255347777, prompt 12563 of YouMind’s Opus 5.5 collection): a floating island with a campfire, rain and moonlight, drawn on an HTML canvas from TypeScript. AwwO’s version adds a wolf cub by the fire that howls at the moon once in every loop (AwwO is said “ah-woo”). The canvas’s text was written for this film by the operator beforehand: the Director’s task (the prompt adapted to AwwO and the look), the kernel contract every module writes to, each builder’s duty, and the tester’s and the editor’s tasks. What is seen and heard is what the canvas’s agents wrote; the builders’ tasks asked for TypeScript compiled in their sandbox computers, and the page holds the JavaScript they delivered. The canvas ran three times, each run after the first running only the nodes it named, on the kept outputs of the rest. The first (09:30 to 09:48 UTC) finished everything but the edit: the render worker then live could not yet record a page’s sound, so the edit refused the timeline’s music (the worker took page sounds from 09:51 UTC). The second (09:59 to 10:03) ran the edit again, which rendered each of the editor’s four pieces from the page and recorded the page’s own sound (window.renderAudio), with no model: the film here. The third ran only the canvas’s Review node, which is not part of this case. The tester found 13 of the page’s 13 tests passing and all 4 planted failures caught, and fixed nothing.",
